to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the saving throw, and only half damage if you fail.\n\nNivel 7 - Evasion\n\nPagina: 129\n\nYou can nimbly dodge out of the way of certain dangers. When you're subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the saving throw and only half damage if you fail. You can't use this feature if you have the XPHB condition.\n\nNivel 7 - Reliable Talent\n\nPagina: 130\n\nWhenever you make an ability check that uses one of your skill or tool proficiencies, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.\n\nNivel 7 - Reliable Talent\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 94\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 130\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 9 - Roguish Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 94\n\nAt 9th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype.\n\nNivel 9 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 130\n\nYou gain a feature from your Rogue Subclass.\n\nNivel 10 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 94\n\nWhen you reach 10th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 10 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 130\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 11 - Improved Cunning Strike\n\nPagina: 130\n\nYou can use up to two Cunning Strike effects when you deal Sneak Attack damage, paying the die cost for each effect.\n\nNivel 11 - Reliable Talent\n\nPagina: 94\n\nBy 11th level, you have refined your chosen skills until they approach perfection. Whenever you make an ability check that lets you add your proficiency bonus, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.\n\nNivel 11 - Reliable Talent\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 94\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 13 - Roguish Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 94\n\nAt 13th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype.\n\nNivel 13 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou gain a feature from your Rogue Subclass.\n\nNivel 14 - Blindsense\n\nPagina: 94\n\nStarting at 14th level, if you are able to hear, you are aware of the location of any hidden or invisible creature within 10 feet of you.\n\nNivel 14 - Blindsense\n\nNivel 14 - Daze (Cost: 2d6)\n\nPagina: 131\n\nThe target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or on its next turn, it can do only one of the following: move or take an action or a XPHB.\n\nNivel 14 - Daze (Cost: 2d6)\n\nNivel 14 - Devious Strikes\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou've practiced new ways to use your Sneak Attack deviously. The following effects are now among your Cunning Strike options.\n\nNivel 14 - Knock Out (Cost: 6d6)\n\nPagina: 131\n\nThe target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw, or it has the XPHB condition for 1 minute or until it takes any damage. The XPHB target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nNivel 14 - Knock Out (Cost: 6d6)\n\nNivel 14 - Obscure (Cost: 3d6)\n\nPagina: 131\n\nThe target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw, or it has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\nNivel 14 - Obscure (Cost: 3d6)\n\nNivel 15 - Slippery Mind\n\nPagina: 94\n\nBy 15th level, you have acquired greater mental strength. You gain proficiency in Wisdom saving throws.\n\nNivel 15 - Slippery Mind\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYour cunning mind is exceptionally difficult to control. You gain proficiency in Wisdom and Charisma saving throws.\n\nNivel 15 - Slippery Mind\n\nNivel 15 - Slippery Mind\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 94\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 17 - Roguish Archetype feature\n\nPagina: 94\n\nAt 17th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype.\n\nNivel 17 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou gain a feature from your Rogue Subclass.\n\nNivel 18 - Elusive\n\nPagina: 94\n\nBeginning at 18th level, you are so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No attack roll has advantage against you while you aren't incapacitated.\n\nNivel 18 - Elusive\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou're so evasive that attackers rarely gain the upper hand against you. No attack roll can have XPHB against you unless you have the XPHB condition.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 94\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Stroke of Luck\n\nPagina: 94\n\nAt 20th level, you have an uncanny knack for succeeding when you need to. If your attack misses a target within range, you can turn the miss into a hit. Alternatively, if you fail an ability check, you can treat the d20 roll as a 20.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 20 - Stroke of Luck\n\nPagina: 131\n\nYou have a marvelous knack for succeeding when you need to. If you fail a XPHB, you can turn the roll into a 20.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB or XPHB.\n\nNivel 20 - Stroke of Luck"},
  ["magicitem.rogue-card.bmt2014"]={title="Rogue Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhen you hit a target with a weapon attack while holding this card, you can deal an extra 6d6 force damage to that target. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.rogue-subclass.xphb2024.rogue.base.3"]={title="Rogue Subclass",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 129\n\nYou gain a Rogue subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Rogue levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Rogue level or lower."},
  ["magicitem.rogue-s-mantle.bmt2014"]={title="Rogue's Mantle",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis dark, hooded mantle of thick cloth is infused with secretive and deceptive magic. While wearing it, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Darkvision You gain darkvision within a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, the mantle increases your darkvision's range by 60 feet instead.\n\n• Move in Shadows While you are in Vision and Light or darkness, you can use a bonus action to teleport, along with anything you are wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in Vision and Light or darkness. You then have advantage on the first melee attack you make before the end of the turn.\n\n• Willful Enmity You can cast the BMT spell (save 15) from the mantle. Once the mantle has cast the spell, it can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype.phb2014.rogue.base.3"]={title="Roguish Archetype",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 3rd level, you choose an archetype that you emulate in the exercise of your rogue abilities from the list of available archetypes. Your archetype choice grants you features at 3rd level and then again at 9th, 13th, and 17th level."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.9"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 9th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.13"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 13th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.17"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 17th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["deity.roknar.mtf2014"]={title="Roknar",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 73"},
  ["traphazard.rolling-sphere.dmg2014"]={title="Rolling Sphere",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\nWhen 20 or more pounds of pressure are placed on this trap's pressure plate, a hidden trapdoor in the ceiling opens, releasing a 10-foot-diameter rolling sphere of solid stone.\n\nWith a successful 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, a character can spot the trapdoor and pressure plate.\n\nA search of the floor accompanied by a successful 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check reveals variations in the mortar and stone that betray the pressure plate's presence. The same check made while inspecting the ceiling notes variations in the stonework that reveal the trapdoor. Wedging an iron spike or other object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from activating.\n\nActivation of the sphere requires all creatures present to roll initiative. The sphere rolls initiative with a +8 bonus. On its turn, it moves 60 feet in a straight line.\n\nThe sphere can move through creatures' spaces, and creatures can move through its space, treating it as difficult terrain. Whenever the sphere enters a creature's space or a creature enters its space while it's rolling, that creature must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 55 (10d10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone.\n\nThe sphere stops when it hits a wall or similar barrier. It can't go around corners, but smart dungeon builders incorporate gentle, curving turns into nearby passages that allow the sphere to keep moving.\n\nAs an action, a creature within 5 feet of the sphere can attempt to slow it down with a 20 Strength check. On a successful check, the sphere's speed is reduced by 15 feet. If the sphere's speed drops to 0, it stops moving and is no longer a threat."},
  ["traphazard.rolling-stone.xdmg2024"]={title="Rolling Stone",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 102\n\nWhen a creature moves onto a hidden pressure plate, a 5-foot-radius orb of solid stone is released from a secret compartment and begins to roll. The stone and all creatures nearby roll Initiative; the stone gets a +8 bonus on its Initiative roll.\n\nOn its turn, the stone moves 60 feet in one direction, changing course if redirected by an obstacle. The stone can move through creatures' spaces, and creatures can move through the stone's space, treating it as XPHB. Whenever the stone enters a creature's space for the first time on a turn or a creature enters the stone's space while the stone is rolling, that creature must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 55 (10d10) Bludgeoning damage and have the XPHB condition.\n\nThe stone stops when it hits a wall or similar barrier. It can't go around corners, but creative dungeon builders incorporate curving turns into nearby passages that allow the stone to keep moving.\n\nDetect and Disarm\n\nAs a XPHB action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pressure plate and make a 15 Intelligence (XPHB) check, deducing the pressure plate's function on a successful check. Wedging an Iron Spike or a similar object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from triggering.\n\nDestroy the Stone\n\nThe stone is a Large object that has AC 17, HP 100, a XPHB of 10, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\nSlow the Stone\n\nAs an action, a creature can try to slow down the stone with a 20 Strength (XPHB) check. If the check is successful, the distance the stone moves on its turn is reduced by 15 feet. If that distance drops to 0, it stops moving and is no longer a threat."},
  ["creature.ront.oota2014"]={title="Ront",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.rool.skt2014"]={title="Rool",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.rooster.jttrc2014"]={title="Rooster",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10"},
  ["item.rope.xphb2024"]={title="Rope",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can tie a knot with Rope if you succeed on a 10 Dexterity (XPHB) check. The Rope can be burst with a successful 20 Strength (XPHB) check.\n\nYou can bind an unwilling creature with the Rope only if the creature has the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition. If the creature's legs are bound, the creature has the XPHB condition until it escapes. Escaping the Rope requires the creature to make a successful 15 Dexterity (XPHB) check as an action."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-climbing.dmg2014"]={title="Rope of Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis 60-foot length of silk rope weighs 3 pounds and can hold up to 3,000 pounds. If you hold one end of the rope and use an action to speak the command word, the rope animates. As a bonus action, you can command the other end to move toward a destination you choose. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet on each of your turns until reaching its destination, up to its maximum length away, or until you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or to unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying.\n\nIf you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. While knotted, the rope shortens to a 50-foot length and grants advantage on checks made to climb it.\n\nThe rope has AC 20 and 20 hit points. It regains 1 hit point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 hit point. If the rope drops to 0 hit points, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-climbing.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 301\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis 60-foot length of rope can hold up to 3,000 pounds. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a XPHB action to command the other end of the rope to animate and move toward a destination you choose, up to the rope's length away from you. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet at the start of each of your subsequent turns until reaching its destination or until you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or to unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying.\n\nIf you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. While knotted, the rope shortens to a 50-foot length and grants XPHB on ability checks made to climb using the rope.\n\nThe rope has AC 20, HP 20, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 XPHB every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 XPHB. If the rope drops to 0 XPHB, it is destroyed.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-entanglement.dmg2014"]={title="Rope of Entanglement",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis rope is 30 feet long and weighs 3 pounds. If you hold one end of the rope and use an action to speak its command word, the other end darts forward to entangle a creature you can see within 20 feet of you. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or become restrained.\n\nYou can release the creature by using a bonus action to speak a second command word. A target restrained by the rope can use an action to make a 15 Strength or Dexterity check (target's choice). On a success, the creature is no longer restrained by the rope.\n\nThe rope has AC 20 and 20 hit points. It regains 1 hit point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 hit point. If the rope drops to 0 hit points, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-entanglement.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Entanglement",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 301\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis rope is 30 feet long. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a XPHB action to command the other end to dart forward and entangle one creature you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition. You can release the target by letting go of your end of the rope (causing the rope to coil up in the target's space) or by using a XPHB to repeat the command (causing the rope to coil up in your hand).\n\nA target XPHB by the rope can take an action to make its choice of a 15 Strength (XPHB) or Dexterity (XPHB) check. On a successful check, the target is no longer XPHB by the rope. If you're still holding onto the rope when a target escapes from it, you can take a XPHB to command the rope to coil up in your hand; otherwise, the rope coils up in the target's space.\n\nThe rope has AC 20, HP 20, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 XPHB every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 XPHB. If the rope drops to 0 XPHB, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-mending.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Mending",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis 50-foot coil of rope can repair itself when cut into any number of smaller pieces. As a XPHB action, you can cause all pieces of the rope that are in contact with each other and not otherwise in use to knit back together. A Rope of Mending is forever shortened if a section of it is lost or destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-mending.xge2024"]={title="Rope of Mending",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can cut this 50-foot coil of hempen rope into any number of smaller pieces, and then use an action to speak a command word and cause the pieces to knit back together. The pieces must be in contact with each other and not otherwise in use. A rope of mending is forever shortened if a section of it is lost or destroyed."},
  ["spell.rope-trick.phb2014"]={title="Rope Trick",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nYou touch a length of rope that is up to 60 feet long. One end of the rope then rises into the air until the whole rope hangs perpendicular to the ground. At the upper end of the rope, an invisible entrance opens to an extradimensional space that lasts until the spell ends.\n\nThe extradimensional space can be reached by climbing to the top of the rope. The space can hold as many as eight Medium or smaller creatures. The rope can be pulled into the space, making the rope disappear from view outside the space.\n\nAttacks and spells can't cross through the entrance into or out of the extradimensional space, but those inside can see out of it as if through a 3-foot-by-5-foot window centered on the rope.\n\nAnything inside the extradimensional space drops out when the spell ends."},
  ["spell.rope-trick.xphb2024"]={title="Rope Trick",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 312\n\nYou touch a rope. One end of it hovers upward until the rope hangs perpendicular to the ground or the rope reaches a ceiling. At the rope's upper end, an XPHB 3-foot-by-5-foot portal opens to an extradimensional space that lasts until the spell ends. That space can be reached by climbing the rope, which can be pulled into or dropped out of it.\n\nThe space can hold up to eight Medium or smaller creatures. Attacks, spells, and other effects can't pass into or out of the space, but creatures inside it can see through the portal. Anything inside the space drops out when the spell ends."},
  ["creature.roper.mm2014"]={title="Roper",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 16 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the roper remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal cave formation, such as a stalagmite.\n\nGrasping Tendrils\n\nThe roper can have up to six tendrils at a time. Each tendril can be attacked (AC 20; 10 hit points; immunity to poison and psychic damage). Destroying a tendril deals no damage to the roper, which can extrude a replacement tendril on its next turn. A tendril can also be broken if a creature takes an action and succeeds on a 15 Strength check against it.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe roper can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe roper makes four attacks with its tendrils, uses Reel, and makes one attack with its bite.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h22 (4d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nTendril\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 50 ft., one creature. hThe target is grappled (escape 15). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained and has disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws, and the roper can't use the same tendril on another target.\n\nReel\n\nThe roper pulls each creature grappled by it up to 25 feet straight toward it."},
  ["creature.roper.xmm2024"]={title="Roper",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 16 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe roper can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe roper makes two Tentacle attacks, uses Reel, and makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h17 (3d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nTentacle\n\nm 7, reach 60 ft. hThe target has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of six tentacles, and the target has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\nThe tentacle can be damaged, freeing a creature it has XPHB when destroyed (AC 20, HP 10, XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage). Damaging the tentacle deals no damage to the roper, and a destroyed tentacle regrows at the start of the roper's next turn.\n\nReel\n\nThe roper pulls each creature XPHB by it up to 30 feet straight toward it."},
  ["creature.rosavalda-rose-durst.cos2014"]={title="Rosavalda \"Rose\" Durst",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 3\n\nPV: 35 (10d6)\n\nIdiomas: Common"},
  ["creature.rosie-beestinger.ai2014"]={title="Rosie Beestinger",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (10d6 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nRosie has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nHalfling Nimbleness\n\nRosie can move through the space of any creature that is of a size larger than hers.\n\nEvasion\n\nIf Rosie is subjected to an effect that allows her to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, she instead takes no damage if she succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if she fails. She can't use this trait if she's incapacitated.\n\nShadow Step\n\nWhen Rosie is in dim light or darkness, she can use a bonus action to teleport 60 feet to an unoccupied space she can see that is also in dim light or darkness. She then has advantage on the first melee attack she makes before the end of the turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRosie makes three attacks, then makes two unarmed strike attacks.\n\nStaff of the Master (+1 Quarterstaff)\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage. Rosie's unarmed strikes are magical.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Missiles\n\nIn response to being hit by a ranged weapon attack, Rosie deflects the missile. The damage she takes from the attack is reduced by 1d10 + 9. If the damage is reduced to 0, she catches the missile if it's small enough to hold in one hand and she has a hand free."},
  ["feature.rot-and-violence.rhw2014.ranger.hollow-warden.11"]={title="Rot and Violence",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nYour dedication to wild eldritch beings alters you further. When transformed using Wrath of the Wild, you gain the following additional benefits.\n\nMenacing Aura\n\nWhen a creature fails its saving throw against your Unnerving Aura, it also can't regain XPHB or take XPHB until the start of your next turn.\n\nStrangling Roots\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon, you can activate the Sap or Slow mastery property in addition to a different mastery property you're using with that weapon."},
  ["traphazard.rot-grub.vgm2014"]={title="Rot Grub",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRot grubs are finger-sized maggots that eat living and dead creatures, although they can survive on vegetation. They infest corpses and piles of decaying matter and attack anyone that disturbs them. After burrowing into a creature, rot grubs instinctively chew their way toward vital parts.\n\nRot grubs recoil from flames, and fire is the main weapon against rot grubs once they're inside a body. Magic that neutralizes poison can also stop them before they kill their host.\n\nSingle Rot Grub\n\nRot grubs pose a threat both singly and as a swarm. See the MPMM for the mechanics of a swarm of rot grubs. A single rot grub has no stat block.\n\nAny creature that comes into contact with a single rot grub must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned, as the rot grub burrows into the creature. The poisoned creature takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the end of each of its turns. Whenever the poisoned creature takes fire damage, the creature can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the poisoned creature ends its turn with 0 hit points, it dies, as the rot grub kills it."},
  ["creature.rot-troll.mpmm2014"]={title="Rot Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRancid Degeneration\n\nAt the end of each of the troll's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 11 (2d10) necrotic damage, unless the troll has taken acid or fire damage since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.rot-troll.mtf2014"]={title="Rot Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRancid Degeneration\n\nAt the end of each of the troll's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 11 (2d10) necrotic damage, unless the troll has taken acid or fire damage since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.rothe.coa2014"]={title="Rothé",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the rothé moved at least 20 feet straight towards this target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.rothe.vgm2014"]={title="Rothé",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the rothé moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.rotor-of-return.ai2014"]={title="Rotor of Return",subtitle="Item Magico - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile attuned to this device, you have a +1 bonus to Constitution saving throws. You periodically receive flashbacks of old memories, and you can unerringly recall any event that took place within the previous 30 days.\n\nBorrow Object\n\nYou name a mundane item with a value of 50 gp or less and it appears in your hand or at your feet. This can be any item that appears in chapter 5, \"PHB,\" of the Player's Handbook, or any similar item selected with the DM's permission. The summoned item is transported to you from somewhere else in the world, but it is generic in nature, so that you might call for a longsword but you cannot borrow a specific creature's longsword. The item vanishes 10 minutes after it appears. Once you use this feature of the rotor of return, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nRecall Code\n\nAs an action, you can set your current location as a point of return locked to the rotor. Anytime thereafter, you can use a bonus action to teleport to the rotor's point of return as long as you are within 500 feet of that point. Once you use the rotor of return to teleport, this feature cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nPart of a Whole\n\nWhile this component is not installed in the AI, its magic might function sporadically or with unpredictable side effects, as determined by the DM."},
  ["creature.rotter.rtg2014"]={title="Rotter",subtitle="Criatura - RtG - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Club\n\nIn the rotter's hand, its club is magical and deals 7 (3d4) extra damage (included in its attacks).\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe rotter has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe rotter regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it is in contact with the ground. If the rotter takes fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the rotter's next turn. The rotter dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nShared Senses\n\nThe rotter can see and hear what any plant within 120 ft can see and hear. In addition, the rotter can communicate telepathically with any plant within this range.\n\nTree Stride\n\nOnce on each of its turns, the rotter can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one copse of mushrooms within 5 feet of it and emerge from a second copse of mushrooms within 60 feet of it, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second copse. Both copses of mushrooms must be Large or bigger. The rotter doesn't need to be able to see the second copse to use this ability.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe rotter makes two attacks with its club.\n\nClub\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["language.roushoum.scag2014"]={title="Roushoum",subtitle="Idioma - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nOption: Human Languages\n\nMany human ethnicities and nations in Faerûn have their own language, in addition to Common. Most human languages are written in Thorass, the alphabet of Old Common, derived from the Chondathan language that traders used as their common tongue. A few human languages use other alphabets, including Draconic, Dethek, and Espruar.\n\nIf your Dungeon Master allows this option, then any human from an ethnic group that has its own language is assumed to know that language as well as Common. This ethnic language is treated as a free additional language for such individuals."},
  ["feature.roving.xphb2024.ranger.base.6"]={title="Roving",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.rowboat.dmg2014"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: none\n\nKeelboats and rowboats are used on lakes and rivers, If going downstream, add the speed of the current (typically 3 miles per hour) to the speed of the vehicle. These vehicles can't be rowed against any significant current, but they can be pulled upstream by draft animals on the shores. A rowboat weighs 100 pounds, in case adventurers carry it over land."},
  ["vehicle.rowboat.gos2014"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Veiculo - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\nOn its turn, the rowboat can take the move action below. It can't take this action if it has no crew.\n\n• Move"},
  ["item.rowboat.xphb2024"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.rowboat-mimic.wdmm2014"]={title="Rowboat Mimic",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: L\n\nPV: 67 (9d10 + 18)"},
  ["feature.royal-envoy.scag2014.fighter.purple-dragon-knight-banneret.7"]={title="Royal Envoy",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.rubblebelt-stalker.ggr2014"]={title="Rubblebelt Stalker",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 239\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmbusher\n\nIn the first round of a combat, the stalker has advantage on attack rolls against any creature that hasn't taken a turn yet.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe stalker can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\nRuin Dweller\n\nThe stalker has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in ruins, and its speed is not reduced in difficult terrain composed of rubble.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe stalker deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe stalker makes three attacks with its shortsword.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["item.ruby.dmg2014"]={title="Ruby",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent clear red to deep crimson gemstone."},
  ["item.ruby.xdmg2024"]={title="Ruby",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA clear red to deep crimson gemstone."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-of-the-war-mage.xdmg2024"]={title="Ruby of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nEtched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby allows you to use a Simple or Martial weapon as a XPHB for your spells. For this property to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing the ruby against it for at least 10 minutes. Thereafter, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as a XPHB action, the weapon is destroyed, or your XPHB to the ruby ends."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-of-the-war-mage.xge2024"]={title="Ruby of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nEtched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby allows you to use a items as a spellcasting focus for your spells. For this property to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing the ruby against it for at least 10 minutes. Thereafter, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as an action or the weapon is destroyed. Not even an antimagic field causes it to fall off. The ruby does fall off the weapon if your attunement to the ruby ends."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-rod-of-asmodeus.coa2014"]={title="Ruby Rod of Asmodeus",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 274\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nAsmodeus's Ruby Rod is said to have been constructed from a shard of pure evil, a ruby soaked in the blood of the innocents, the drool from a draconic deity, and the tears of 777 angels. It is a magic rod that functions as a morningstar and you have a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. All damage dealt with it is converted to necrotic, and when you hit a good aligned creature, that creature takes an extra 2d12 necrotic damage.\n\nThe Ruby Rod of Asmodeus has 66 charges and regains 6d6 charges each nightfall. Asmodeus is always capable of perceiving through the rod and knows the exact location of any creature attuned to it. If a creature uses the special abilities of the rod without Asmodeus's permission, they take 2d12 necrotic damage each use, doubled if they're good aligned. This damage ignores resistances and immunities, and if it kills the user, Asmodeus permanently claims their soul.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Ruby Rod of Asmodeus has the following random properties:\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\nAsmodeus is immune to the detrimental properties of the weapon.\n\nBow to the King\n\nYou may use an action to expend 33 charges to use the rod to force all creatures within a 150-foot-radius to bow to you. A creature must succeed on a 21 Charisma saving throw or be forced to kneel for up to 1 hour. Creatures immune to the charmed condition have advantage on their save. Each time a kneeling creature takes damage, they may repeat the save, ending the effect on a success. The effect also ends early for kneeling creatures if they're touched by the Ruby Rod.\n\nAcid, Cold, and Lightning\n\nAt a cost of 9 charges each use, you may use an action to trigger one of the following effects:\n\n• You project acid in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 12d8 acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• You project an icy blast in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 12d8 cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• You shoot lightning in a 90-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 12d10 lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nReactions\n\nAs a reaction to suffering a detrimental effect, you may cast Lesser Restoration (expending 3 charges) or Greater Restoration (expending 12 charges.)\n\nAdditionally, if you're the sole target of a spell, you may use a reaction to attempt to use the rod to absorb the spell and cancel its effect. You roll 1d20 + 2, and if the result is higher than the spell level + 10, the spell is absorbed into the rod. The rod regains charges equal to the spell level it absorbed. If the absorbed charges go over the maximum of 66 charges, it overloads, dealing 1d6 necrotic damage per charge to you and expending all charges.\n\nDestroying the Rod\n\nWhile Asmodeus lives, the Ruby Rod of Asmodeus can't be destroyed, and if attempted it simply returns to Asmodeus. If he were defeated, the rod could be destroyed by bringing it to the Abyss from whence it was created, then performing a ritual known only to Asmodeus."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-weave-gem.ftd2014"]={title="Ruby Weave Gem",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhile you are holding this gem, you can use it as a spellcasting focus for your spells.\n\nThe gem has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. When you cast a spell while holding this gem, you can expend up to 3 charges to ignore the spell's material components with a gold piece cost, up to 500 gp per charge expended.\n\nWhen you finish a long rest, choose a spell from any class list. The spell you choose must be of a level you can cast. You know the chosen spell and can cast it with your spell slots of the appropriate level until the end of your next long rest."},
  ["creature.rudolph-van-richten.rhw2014"]={title="Rudolph van Richten",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 105 (14d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 18 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShield of Erasmus\n\nWhile XPHB, Rudolph has XPHB to Force, Poison, and Psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRudolph makes three attacks, using Silver Sword Cane or Hand Crossbow in any combination.\n\nSilver Sword Cane\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 5 (2d4) Radiant damage. Critical hThe target has the XPHB condition until it finishes a XPHB. It makes a 15 Constitution saving throw at end of each hour, ending the effect on a success.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nr 5, range 30/120 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 5 (2d4) Radiant damage.\n\nRepel Evil {@recharge 5}\n\ncha 15, each creature of Rudolph's choice in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of Rudolph's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nOccult Aid (2/Day)\n\nRudolph casts XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB, using Wisdom as the spellcasting modifier (spell save 15)."},
  ["creature.rudolph-von-aubrecker.pl2014"]={title="Rudolph von Aubrecker",subtitle="Criatura - PL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nForcefield Generator\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRudolph makes one Taser attack and uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB.\n\nTaser\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h14 (4d6) Lightning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Rudolph's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nX-Ray Scanning\n\nRudolph gains Blindsight to a range of 60 feet. This Blindsight ignores XPHB created by up to 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances or thin sheets of lead block the Blindsight as usual. This benefit lasts for 1 minute or until Rudolph has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.rug-of-smothering.mm2014"]={title="Rug of Smothering",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 33 (6d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe rug is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the rug must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nDamage Transfer\n\nWhile it is grappling a creature, the rug takes only half the damage dealt to it, and the creature grappled by the rug takes the other half.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the rug remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal rug.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. hThe creature is grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, blinded, and at risk of suffocating, and the rug can't smother another target. In addition, at the start of each of the target's turns, the target takes 10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ruidium-elephant.crcotn2014"]={title="Ruidium Elephant",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 9 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTrampling Charge\n\nIf the elephant moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a Gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the elephant can make one Stomp attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 10 to hit (with advantage if the target is a creature missing any hit points), reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (4d8 + 7) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage."},
  ["magicitem.ruidium-shield.crcotn2014"]={title="Ruidium Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nTendrils of ruidium extend across the metal surface of this shield. While this shield is on your person, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You have resistance to psychic damage.\n\n• You can breathe water.\n\n• You gain a swimming speed equal to your walking speed.\n\nPsychic Reflection\n\nWhen you take psychic damage while holding the shield, you can use your reaction to choose another creature you can see within 30 feet of you. That creature takes the psychic damage you would have taken.\n\nRuidium Corruption\n\nWhen you use the shield's Psychic Reflection property, you must make a 20 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, you gain 1 level of exhaustion. If you are not already suffering from ruidium corruption, you become corrupted when you fail this save.\n\nIf Ruidium Is Destroyed\n\nIf the Apotheon is killed or redeemed, all the ruidium in Exandria is destroyed instantly, and a ruidium shield becomes a +2 shield."},
  ["magicitem.ruin-card.bmt2014"]={title="Ruin Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can brandish this card and use it to cast the Disintegrate spell (save 17). Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.ruin-grinder.scc2014"]={title="Ruin Grinder",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 82 (11d10 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Absorption\n\nWhenever the ruin grinder is subjected to fire damage, it regains a number of hit points equal to half the fire damage dealt.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe ruin grinder deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe ruin grinder can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ruin grinder makes two Excavator attacks.\n\nExcavator\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) force damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away and knocked prone."},
  ["creature.ruin-spider.bmt2014"]={title="Ruin Spider",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 105 (14d10 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRuinous Acid\n\nAny nonmagical weapon that hits the spider corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to -5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the spider is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe spider can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Sense\n\nWhile in contact with a web, the spider knows the exact location of any other creature in contact with the same web.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe spider ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spider makes two Ruinous Bite attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Web.\n\nRuinous Bite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage and 9 (2d8) acid damage. In addition, if the target is a creature wearing nonmagical armor, the armor takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it offers. Armor reduced to an Armor Class of 10 is destroyed.\n\nWeb {@recharge 5}\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one creature. hThe target has the restrained condition. As an action, a restrained target can make a 13 Strength check, bursting the webbing on a successful check. The webbing can also be destroyed (AC 10; 5 hit points; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to acid, bludgeoning, poison, and psychic damage)."},
  ["item.ruin-s-wake-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.ruin-s-wake-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThis spear is made from the ivory bone of an ancient gold dragon and carved with an Orc hymn to Gruumsh.\n\nSentience\n\nRuin's Wake is a sentient chaotic evil weapon with an Intelligence of 20, a Wisdom of 16, and a Charisma of 22. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Abyssal, Common, and Orc.\n\nPersonality\n\nA slaughter-loving balor named Yarrowish lives within Ruin's Wake. The weapon desires only to draw blood and pushes its wielder to solve problems with violence.\n\nDormant\n\nThe spear grants the following benefits in its dormant state:\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Abyssal and Orc.\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, and it deals an extra 1d8 piercing damage to any target it hits. Immediately after you make a ranged attack with this weapon, it flies back to your hand.\n\n• As a reaction when you are hit by a melee attack, you can make a melee attack with Ruin's Wake with advantage against the attacker. You can't use this property again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nBetrayer Artifact Properties\n\nThe Arms of the Betrayers advance in power in the same manner as the Vestiges of Divergence. In its dormant state, each of these artifacts has one dmg property and one dmg property. When the artifact attains an awakened state, it gains an additional dmg property and an additional dmg property. When the item reaches its exalted state, it gains a dmg property. See \"Artifact Properties\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for more information."},
  ["item.ruin-s-wake-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.ruinblade.imr2014"]={title="Ruinblade",subtitle="Item Magico - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nRuinblade is a unique weapon possessed by IMR, the architect of the Tomb of Horrors. A symbol of his authority, Moghadam carries the weapon during the time frame of the adventure to intimidate the tomb's workers. (In later years, after ToA trapped Moghadam in the completed tomb as an undead archwraith, Moghadam was able to use the weapon as his own phylactery.)\n\nA small jade version of the green devil face of the Tomb of Horrors is fashioned into the hilt of the weapon, with the blade extending from its open mouth. The blade always appears ruined and rusting, and causes its surroundings to appear reflected in the blade as if in a state of decay.\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit an undead creature with it, the attack deals an extra 1d8 force damage.\n\nIn addition, the weapon has the following properties:\n\nBlighted Ruin\n\nYou can cast the blight spell from the weapon (15). Once used, this property of the weapon can't be used until the next dawn.\n\nDestructive Ruin\n\nYou can cast the disintegrate spell from the weapon, but can target only a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force. Once used, this property of the weapon can't be used until dawn seven days later.\n\nCurse\n\nThis weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. Until the curse is broken with a remove curse spell or similar magic, you are unwilling to part with the weapon.\n\nThe weapon must take direct part in the destruction of 1,000 gp worth of materials and objects every seven days, or a conflict arises between you and the weapon at the end of the seventh day.\n\nSentience\n\nRuinblade is a sentient lawful evil weapon with an Intelligence of 15, a Wisdom of 8, and a Charisma of 16. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon can speak, read, and understand Common, and can communicate with its wielder telepathically. Its voice is a rough, ruined echo. While you are attuned to it, Ruinblade also understands every language you know.\n\nPersonality\n\nRuinblade speaks either with a dolorous or frenetic tone, depending on its mood. That mood improves when the sword is actively engaged in acts of destruction, but worsens if the blade is left inactive too long.\n\nThe weapon's purpose is to ruin and unmake existing objects, so that its owner can rebuild the world from a blank slate. It thus encourages its wielder to engage in constant destruction, claiming that this will allow the creation of a more superior vision from the ruin of what came before."},
  ["background.ruined.bmt2014"]={title="Ruined",subtitle="Background - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 58\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies: One items of your choice (such as playing cards or three-dragon ante cards)\n\nFeature: Still Standing\n\nYou have weathered ruinous misfortune, and you possess hidden reserves others don't expect. You gain the Alert, Skilled, or Tough feat (your choice). Your choice of feat reflects how you've dealt with the terrible loss that changed your life forever. If you've kept your senses sharp for every opportunity and climbed your way out of misery by seizing the tiniest scrap of hope, choose Alert. If you've redoubled your efforts to reclaim what was once yours, choose Skilled. If you've stoically persevered through your misfortune, select Tough.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nRising above misfortune shapes one's perspective. The Ruined Personality Traits table suggests traits you might adopt for your character (and ruinous cards that might have prompted this trait).\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I've changed from my past, and I work to live up to my new path. (Balance, Throne)\n\n2 | Every moment is a gift I refuse to squander. (Euryale, Skull)\n\n3 | Now that I've overcome having nothing, I can survive anything. (Fool, Ruin, Talons)\n\n4 | I know enemies are set against me, and I always prepare for the worst. (Flames, Rogue)\n\n5 | I interpret every event as part of a larger pattern I just haven't worked out yet. (Puzzle, Star)\n\n6 | I must make up for so much time I've already lost. (Donjon, Void)\n\nBuilding a Ruined Character\n\nRuined characters were on top of the world before misfortune struck. Many were wealthy. Others come from modest backgrounds, but they were surrounded by friends, family, and loved ones. They might have been famous, or simply never encountered serious hardship before. Some were born to privilege or rose to prominence through trickery or a false reputation. Now a Deck of Many Things—or another calamity—has knocked them down like a house of cards.\n\nIf your character's life was ruined by a Deck of Many Things, consider which card was responsible. Perhaps your character was imprisoned for years by the Donjon or Void card, and now everyone they knew has died. Maybe your character drew the Rogue card, and the person closest to them—a spouse, child, or parent—turned against them. A devil unleashed by the Flames card might have destroyed their life. The Ruin or Talons card might have stolen the character's material goods or saddled them with vast debt.\n\nRuined Trinkets\n\nWhen you make your character, you can roll once on the Ruined Trinkets table instead of on the Trinkets table in the PHB.\n\nd6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A rusted scrap of a once-beloved family heirloom\n\n2 | A land deed, but all the names and markings that once tied it to you have faded into obscurity\n\n3 | A bauble once imbued with powerful magic\n\n4 | A battered playing card with a hole pierced in it, its face depicting the card that affected you\n\n5 | A yellowed Humanoid tooth that whispers eerily when placed under a pillow\n\n6 | A keepsake from someone you were once close to but who is now your enemy"},
  ["magicitem.ruinous-flail.bmt2014"]={title="Ruinous Flail",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis ash-gray flail is cold to the touch. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, and it deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nAdditionally, when you hit a creature with this weapon, you can force the creature to make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature has the poisoned condition for 1 minute. The poisoned creature takes 2d4 necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Once this property is used in this way, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.ruinstone.dc2014"]={title="Ruinstone",subtitle="Item Magico - DC - 2014",body="Raridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nA fiery red crystal the size of a human palm.\n\nOnce per day as a bonus action, a villain can activate the ruinstone to undo one deed they have performed. The possibilities here are broad, but in combat it's simplest to allow them the opportunity to \"rewind\" one action and take it again, or to reroll a failed saving throw (if it can still take actions).\n\nEach use of the artifact has a terrible side effect: someone known to the wielder is also erased from reality. After the villain uses the ruinstone, roll a d20: on a 5-20, one of their allies disintegrates, on an 1-4, one of the player characters disintegrates.\n\nIf a creature bound its soul to the ruinstone in the \"Thalivar's Beacon\" quest, the artifact explodes when used and the creature who is bound to it disintegrates, disappearing from reality and can only be brought back with a wish spell, or similar magic."},
  ["creature.rumpadump.oota2014"]={title="Rumpadump",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.runara.dosi2014"]={title="Runara",subtitle="Criatura - DoSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 13"},
  ["charoption.runaway-author.idrotf2014"]={title="Runaway Author",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nI penned a notorious exposé called \"The Hellbent Highborn,\" which accused several prominent patriars in Baldur's Gate and nobles in Waterdeep of being devil worshipers. Although my accusations were well founded, I made a lot of enemies and was forced to seek refuge in Icewind Dale."},
  ["background.rune-carver.bgg2014"]={title="Rune Carver",subtitle="Background - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nRune Styles\n\nEach rune carver has a unique style and preferred medium. To determine how you make your runes, you can roll on the Rune Style table.\n\nd6 | Style\n\n1 | You inscribe runes in wax or clay with a fine metal needle.\n\n2 | You whittle pieces of wood into small figurines you mark with runes.\n\n3 | You engrave runes onto glass beads and thread them onto necklaces and bracelets.\n\n4 | You stitch runes into the hems of clothing.\n\n5 | You carve runes on a set of animal bones you can throw in different formations.\n\n6 | You draw runes into candles, melting the wax to smooth over the engravings.\n\nBuilding a Rune Carver Character\n\nScholarly pursuits, ancient mysteries, or a fateful encounter might inspire a character to pursue the secrets of a rune carver.\n\nFeature: Rune Shaper\n\nYou gain the BGG feat.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nThe Rune Carver Personality Traits table suggests a variety of traits you might adopt for your character.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | Is it practical to learn an ancient language that is rarely spoken? No. But is it fun? Very.\n\n2 | I learned one of my ancestors was a lauded rune carver whose story was lost to time. I seek to rekindle that legacy.\n\n3 | The old, traditional markings of runecraft look so boring. Why not give my runes some flair?\n\n4 | In my studies of runes, I strive to understand how great civilizations of the past fell, so I can prevent it from happening to societies of the present.\n\n5 | Life may be a whirlwind of chaos, but whenever I create my runes, I feel at peace.\n\n6 | My brain struggles to process words written in ink, but the feeling of carved runes makes my mind sing."},
  ["feature.rune-carver.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.3"]={title="Rune Carver",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\n\nFighter Level | Number of Runes\n\n3rd | 2\n\n7th | 3\n\n10th | 4\n\n15th | 5\n\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier."},
  ["subclass.rune-knight.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.0"]={title="Rune Knight",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiencies\n\nPagina: 44\n\n3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou gain proficiency with PHB, and you learn to speak, read, and write Giant.\n\nNivel 3 - Bonus Proficiencies\n\nNivel 3 - Giant's Might\n\nPagina: 44\n\n3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou have learned how to imbue yourself with the might of giants. As a bonus action, you magically gain the following benefits, which last for 1 minute:\n\n• If you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If you lack the room to become Large, your size doesn't change.\n\n• You have advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\n• Once on each of your turns, one of your attacks with a weapon or an unarmed strike can deal an extra 1d6 damage to a target on a hit.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Rune Carver\n\nPagina: 44\n\n3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\n\nFighter Level | Number of Runes\n\n3rd | 2\n\n7th | 3\n\n10th | 4\n\n15th | 5\n\nThe following runes are available to you when you learn a rune. If a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.\n\nHill Rune (7th Level or Higher)\n\nStorm Rune (7th Level or Higher)\n\nNivel 3 - Rune Carver\n\n3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\n\nFighter Level | Number of Runes\n\n3rd | 2\n\n7th | 3\n\n10th | 4\n\n15th | 5\n\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.\n\nNivel 3 - Rune Knight\n\nPagina: 44\n\nRune Knights enhance their martial prowess using the supernatural power of runes, an ancient practice that originated with giants. Rune cutters can be found among any family of giants, and you likely learned your methods first or second hand from such a mystical artisan. Whether you found the giant's work carved into a hill or cave, learned of the runes from a sage, or met the giant in person, you studied the giant's craft and learned how to apply magic runes to empower your equipment.\n\nNivel 7 - Additional Rune Known\n\nPagina: 44\n\n7th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune.\n\nNivel 7 - Runic Shield\n\nPagina: 44\n\n7th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn to invoke your rune magic to protect your allies. When another creature you can see within 60 feet of you is hit by an attack roll, you can use your reaction to force the attacker to reroll the d20 and use the new roll.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 7 - Runic Shield\n\nNivel 10 - Additional Rune Known\n\nPagina: 44\n\n10th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune.\n\nNivel 10 - Great Stature\n\nPagina: 44\n\n10th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nThe magic of your runes permanently alters you. When you gain this feature, roll 3d4. You grow a number of inches in height equal to the roll.\n\nMoreover, the extra damage you deal with your Giant's Might feature increases to 1d8.\n\nNivel 15 - Additional Rune Known\n\nPagina: 44\n\n15th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn an additional Rune.\n\nNivel 15 - Master of Runes\n\nPagina: 44\n\n15th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can invoke each rune you know from your Rune Carver feature twice, rather than once, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a short or long rest.\n\nNivel 18 - Runic Juggernaut\n\nPagina: 44\n\n18th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation. As a result, the extra damage you deal with the Giant's Might feature increases to 1d10. Moreover, when you use that feature, your size can increase to Huge, and while you are that size, your reach increases by 5 feet."},
  ["feature.rune-knight.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.3"]={title="Rune Knight",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nRune Knights enhance their martial prowess using the supernatural power of runes, an ancient practice that originated with giants. Rune cutters can be found among any family of giants, and you likely learned your methods first or second hand from such a mystical artisan. Whether you found the giant's work carved into a hill or cave, learned of the runes from a sage, or met the giant in person, you studied the giant's craft and learned how to apply magic runes to empower your equipment."},
  ["feat.rune-shaper.bgg2014"]={title="Rune Shaper",subtitle="Feat - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nYou've studied the magic of Giant runes, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• Comprehend Languages You learn the comprehend languages spell. You can cast this spell without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast this spell using any spell slots you have.\n\n• Rune Magic You know a number of runes equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded down), chosen from the Rune Spells table. Whenever you finish a long rest, you can inscribe each rune you know onto one nonmagical weapon, armor, piece of clothing, or other object you touch. You temporarily learn the 1st-level spells that correspond to the runes you inscribed, as specified on the Rune Spells table, and you know those spells until you finish a long rest, when the runes fade. While you are wearing or carrying any rune-marked object, you can cast the spells associated with those runes using any spell slots you have. You can also invoke a rune inscribed on an object you are wearing or carrying and cast its associated spell without expending a spell slot or using material components. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest. Your spellcasting ability for this feat is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat). Each time you gain a level, you can replace one of the runes you know with another one from the Rune Spells table. Rune | Spell Cloud | Fog cloud Death | Inflict wounds Dragon | Chromatic orb Enemy | Disguise self Fire | Burning hands Friend | Speak with animals Frost | Armor of Agathys Hill | Goodberry Journey | Longstrider King | Command Mountain | Entangle Stone | Sanctuary Storm | Thunderwave"},
  ["creature.runed-behir.wdmm2014"]={title="Runed Behir",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nLesser Magic\n\nGreater Magic (Costs 2 Actions)"},
  ["creature.runic-colossus.bgg2014"]={title="Runic Colossus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 315 (18d20 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 9 | CON 24 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Giant but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe colossus is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe colossus has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe colossus deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe colossus makes two Slam attacks and then uses Stomp.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h26 (3d12 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or have the prone condition. Until the colossus uses its Stomp again or moves, the creature has the restrained condition. The restrained creature or another creature within 5 feet of it can use its action to make a 22 Strength check. On a successful check, the affected creature relocates to an unoccupied space of its choice within 5 feet of the colossus and is no longer restrained.\n\nArcane Beam {@recharge 5}\n\nThe colossus fires a beam of magical force from its chest, hands, or head in a 150-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 58 (9d12) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpell Reflection (2/Day)\n\nrs 14 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature casting a spell of 5th level or lower. h26 (4d12) force damage, and the target must succeed on a 15 Intelligence saving throw or the spell fails and has no effect."},
  ["feature.runic-juggernaut.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.18"]={title="Runic Juggernaut",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n18th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation. As a result, the extra damage you deal with the Giant's Might feature increases to 1d10. Moreover, when you use that feature, your size can increase to Huge, and while you are that size, your reach increases by 5 feet."},
  ["feature.runic-shield.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.7"]={title="Runic Shield",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.rush-of-the-gale-spirits.phb2014"]={title="Rush of the Gale Spirits",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\nYou can spend 2 ki points to cast gust of wind."},
  ["traphazard.russet-mold.vgm2014"]={title="Russet Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\nFew know for sure where russet mold came from. One historical account tells of adventurers in a mountain range discovering russet mold and bestiary in a peculiar metal dungeon full of strange life. Another story says that explorers found russet mold in a crater left by a falling star, with MPMM infesting the forest nearby.\n\nThe mold is found only in places that are dark, warm, and wet. Russet mold that spreads out across a metal object can be mistaken for rust, and a successful 15 Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check is required to identify it.\n\nEffects of the Mold\n\nAny creature that comes within 5 feet of russet mold must make a 13 Constitution saving throw as the mold emits a puff of spores. On a failed save, the creature is poisoned. While poisoned in this way, the creature takes 7 (2d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Any magic that neutralizes poison or cures disease kills the infestation. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by the mold dies. If the dead creature is a Beast, a Giant, or a Humanoid, one or more vegepygmies emerge from its body 24 hours later: one from a Small corpse, two from a Medium corpse, four from a Large corpse, eight from a Huge corpse, or sixteen from a Gargantuan corpse.\n\nDestroying the Mold\n\nRusset mold can be hard to kill, since weapons and most types of damage do it no harm. Effects that deal acid, necrotic, or radiant damage kill 1 square foot of russet mold per 1 damage dealt. A pound of salt, a gallon of alcohol, or magic that cures disease kills russet mold in a square area that is 10 feet on a side. Sunlight kills any russet mold in the light's area."},
  ["creature.rust-monster.mm2014"]={title="Rust Monster",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIron Scent\n\nThe rust monster can pinpoint, by scent, the location of ferrous metal within 30 feet of it.\n\nRust Metal\n\nAny nonmagical weapon made of metal that hits the rust monster corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Non magical ammunition made of metal that hits the rust monster is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nAntennae\n\nThe rust monster corrodes a nonmagical ferrous metal object it can see within 5 feet of it. If the object isn't being worn or carried, the touch destroys a 1-foot cube of it. If the object is being worn or carried by a creature, the creature can make a 11 Dexterity saving throw to avoid the rust monster's touch.\n\nIf the object touched is either metal armor or a metal shield being worn or carried, it takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to the AC it offers. Armor reduced to an AC of 10 or a shield that drops to a +0 bonus is destroyed. If the object touched is a held metal weapon, it rusts as described in the Rust Metal trait."},
  ["creature.rust-monster.xmm2024"]={title="Rust Monster",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 263\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIron Scent\n\nThe rust monster can pinpoint the location of ferrous metal within 30 feet of itself.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe rust monster makes one Bite attack and uses Antennae twice.\n\nBite\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage.\n\nAntennae\n\nThe rust monster targets one nonmagical metal object—armor or a weapon—worn or carried by a creature within 5 feet of itself. dex 11, the creature with the object. actSaveFail The object takes a -1 penalty to the AC it offers (armor) or to its attack rolls (weapon). Armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10, and a weapon is destroyed if its penalty reaches -5. The penalty can be removed by casting the XPHB spell on the armor or weapon.\n\nDestroy Metal\n\nThe rust monster touches a nonmagical metal object within 5 feet of itself that isn't being worn or carried. The touch destroys a 1-foot XPHB of the object.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReflexive Antennae\n\nactTrigger An attack roll hits the rust monster. actResponse The rust monster uses Antennae."},
  ["creature.rusted-behemoth.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Behemoth",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 157 (15d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes three attacks, using Slam or Rusted Shot Put in any combination.\n\nSlam\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h20 (4d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nRusted Shot Put\n\nr 10, range 60/240 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRust-Riddled Hide\n\nactTrigger The Rusted is hit by an attack roll that deals Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage. dcon 16, each creature of the Rusted's choice in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the Rusted. actSaveFail the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the target's next turn."},
  ["creature.rusted-berserker.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Berserker",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes two attacks, using Greatsword or Javelin in any combination.\n\nGreatsword\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\nJavelin\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["item.rusted-hulk.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Hulk",subtitle="Item - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.rusted-wyrm.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Wyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / G\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 231 (14d20 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 60\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, frightened, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the Rusted fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 12, reach 20 ft. h29 (4d10 + 7) Piercing damage.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 19, each creature and flammable object that isn't being worn or carried in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 45 (7d12) Fire damage, and the target starts XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Being underwater doesn't grant XPHB to this Fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEncasing Rust\n\ncon 19, one creature within 20 feet of the Rusted. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.rutterkin.mpmm2014"]={title="Rutterkin",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmobilizing Fear\n\nWhen a creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet of one or more rutterkins, that creature must make a 11 Wisdom saving throw. The creature has disadvantage on the save if it's within 30 feet of six or more rutterkins. On a failed save, the creature becomes frightened of the rutterkins for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the creature is restrained. At the end of each of the frightened creature's turns, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the Crippling Fear of all rutterkins for 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned. At the end of each long rest, the poisoned target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points while poisoned in this way, it dies and instantly transforms into a living manes. The transformation can be undone only by a wish spell."},
  ["creature.rutterkin.mtf2014"]={title="Rutterkin",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 136\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCrippling Fear\n\nWhen a creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet of three or more rutterkins, it must make a 11 Wisdom saving throw. The creature has disadvantage on the save if it's within 30 feet of six or more rutterkins. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the Crippling Fear of all rutterkins for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature becomes frightened for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the creature is restrained. At the end of each of the frightened creature's turns, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned. At the end of each long rest, the poisoned target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points while poisoned in this way, it dies and instantly transforms into a living mtf. The transformation of the body can be undone only by a wish spell."},
  ["creature.ruxithid-the-chosen.pabtso2014"]={title="Ruxithid the Chosen",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 88 (16d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 19 | CON 12 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nWhen Ruxithid fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMental Fortitude\n\nRuxithid has advantage on saving throws against the charmed and frightened conditions.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRuxithid makes two Psi-Charged Scimitar attacks.\n\nPsi-Charged Scimitar\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBrain Tendrils {@recharge 5}\n\nRuxithid unleashes a flurry of crystalline psychic tendrils from his brain, targeting one creature that he can see within 30 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) psychic damage and have the stunned condition until the start of Ruxithid's next turn.\n\nCombat Command\n\nRuxithid commands one allied creature he can see within 60 feet of himself to strike. The creature can immediately use its reaction to make one melee weapon attack against a target within its reach."},
  ["item.ryath-root.toa2014"]={title="Ryath Root",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nAny creature that ingests a ryath root gains 2d4 temporary hit points. A creature that consumes more than one ryath root in a 24-hour period must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or suffer the poisoned condition for 1 hour."},
  ["creature.rystia-zav.oota2014"]={title="Rystia Zav",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.saber-toothed-tiger.mm2014"]={title="Saber-Toothed Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 336\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe tiger has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPounce\n\nIf the tiger moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the tiger can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.saber-toothed-tiger.xmm2024"]={title="Saber-Toothed Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 369\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRunning Leap\n\nWith a 10-foot running start, the tiger can XPHB up to 25 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tiger makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe tiger takes the XPHB or XPHB action."},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.sack.phb2014"]={title="Sack",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA sack can hold up to 1 cubic foot or 30 pounds of gear."},
  ["item.sack.xphb2024"]={title="Sack",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Sack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot."},
  ["spell.sacred-flame.phb2014"]={title="Sacred Flame",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nFlame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 radiant damage. The target gains no benefit from cover for this saving throw.\n\nThe spell's damage increases by 1d8 when you reach 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8), and 17th level (4d8)."},
  ["spell.sacred-flame.xphb2024"]={title="Sacred Flame",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nFlame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 Radiant damage. The target gains no benefit from XPHB or Three-Quarters XPHB for this save."},
}
